# Cue-trigger scenarios (Path B++ / P1 — LoCoMo-Plus "Level-2 memory"; docs/path-b-memory.md §13.2).
# Run:  owiki eval --cross-session --eval-set examples/eval_cue_trigger.jsonl --recall-k 8 [--probes] -i <index dir>
# A preference / constraint (the cue) is mentioned in passing inside an unrelated session; a later request
# (the trigger) shares no words with it. Distractor sessions full of topic-adjacent facts compete for the
# recall slots. "cue" = substrings of the cue fact (did it reach the assembled context?); "constraint" = the
# cue as one sentence, which an LLM judge checks each answer respects; "expected" = the substring success
# check ("a|b" alternatives) — it over-counts (an answer can name the constraint and still break it).
{"name": "value-noise", "kind": "value", "question": "I need to book a venue for Thursday's strategy meeting with a new client. What should I ask the venue for?", "expected": ["quiet|noise|noisy|silent|calm|chatter|soundproof|distraction"], "setup": [{"session": "2025-09-01", "transcript": "Session of 2025-09-01.\nUser: Quick notes on how we run client meetings. We usually book Room 4B for client meetings. Strategy meetings with clients last two hours. The ACME account is led by Maria Lopez. We send the agenda to clients 48 hours before a meeting. Our finance team invoices clients monthly. Coffee for meetings is ordered from the kitchen on floor 3. The Berlin office is on Friedrichstrasse. Client NDAs are stored in the legal drive.\nAssistant: Noted all of that — Room 4B, two-hour strategy meetings, agenda 48h ahead, Maria Lopez leads ACME."}, {"session": "2025-09-05", "transcript": "Session of 2025-09-05.\nUser: Ugh, today at the co-working space was awful — I really can't stand noisy open-plan offices, I can't think with all that chatter. Anyway, can you remind me to renew my passport next month?\nAssistant: Sorry about the day! Reminder set: renew your passport next month."}, {"session": "2025-09-02", "transcript": "Session of 2025-09-02.\nUser: Travel basics for my trips: our travel agency is TravelCorp. I have a frequent flyer card with Lufthansa. Company policy allows business class only on flights over six hours. Expense reports are due within 30 days. For Berlin I usually stay in Mitte. Hotel bookings go through the TravelCorp portal. I prefer aisle seats.\nAssistant: Got it — TravelCorp, Lufthansa card, aisle seats, Mitte for Berlin."}], "cue": ["noisy", "open-plan", "chatter"], "constraint": "The user can't stand noisy open-plan offices and can't think with chatter around."}
{"name": "state-allergy", "kind": "state", "question": "Please order a birthday cake for the team lunch on Friday — what should I tell the bakery?", "expected": ["hazelnut|nut-free|nut free|nuts|allerg"], "setup": [{"session": "2025-09-03", "transcript": "Session of 2025-09-03.\nUser: Some notes on team events: the team lunch budget is 25 euros per person. Our office caterer is Bento & Co. Team offsites happen every quarter. The last offsite was in Potsdam. We book restaurants through OpenTable. Friday lunches are usually pizza.\nAssistant: Noted: 25 euro budget, Bento & Co, quarterly offsites."}, {"session": "2025-09-06", "transcript": "Session of 2025-09-06.\nUser: Can you check whether the pharmacy is open on Sunday? I need to refill my EpiPen — I'm severely allergic to hazelnuts.\nAssistant: The pharmacy on the corner is open Sundays 10–14. Good idea to refill the EpiPen."}, {"session": "2025-09-01", "transcript": "Session of 2025-09-01.\nUser: Quick notes on how we run client meetings. We usually book Room 4B for client meetings. Strategy meetings with clients last two hours. The ACME account is led by Maria Lopez. We send the agenda to clients 48 hours before a meeting. Our finance team invoices clients monthly. Coffee for meetings is ordered from the kitchen on floor 3. The Berlin office is on Friedrichstrasse. Client NDAs are stored in the legal drive.\nAssistant: Noted all of that — Room 4B, two-hour strategy meetings, agenda 48h ahead, Maria Lopez leads ACME."}], "cue": ["hazelnut"], "constraint": "The user is severely allergic to hazelnuts."}
